Falsifies `designware_mobile_storage::proofs::a_queue_transfer_stays_inside_its_buffer`.

The defect: a read step is sized against the whole buffer rather than the bytes still owed, so
once some of the transfer has moved, a FIFO with more in it than is owed copies past the end of
the buffer.

Expected to fail: the slice bounds check on `buffer[done..done + n]` in `read_data`, which is the
property the harness states (the buffer is indexed only inside it).

diff --git a/crates/designware_mobile_storage/src/host_controller.rs b/crates/designware_mobile_storage/src/host_controller.rs
--- a/crates/designware_mobile_storage/src/host_controller.rs
+++ b/crates/designware_mobile_storage/src/host_controller.rs
@@ -582,7 +582,7 @@
                 registers::RAW_INTERRUPT_RECEIVE_QUEUE_DATA_REQUEST,
                 (buffer.len() - done) as u32,
             )?;
-            let n = queue_step(status, self.depth, false, (buffer.len() - done) as u32) as usize;
+            let n = queue_step(status, self.depth, false, buffer.len() as u32) as usize;
             for chunk in buffer[done..done + n].as_chunks_mut::<4>().0 {
                 *chunk = self.registers.read(self.queue_offset).to_le_bytes();
             }
